  "original_lyrics": "[verse]\nIt was one hundred degrees as we sat beneath willow tree,\nWhose tears didn't care, they just hung in the air, and refused to fall, to fall.\nAnd I knew I' made horrible call. And now the state line felt like the Berlin wall,\nAnd there was no doubt about which side I was on. Hmmm.....\n'Cause I built you home in my heart\nwith rotten wood--it decayed from the start\n'Cause you can't find nothing at all,\nIf there was nothing there all along.\nNo you can't find nothing at all,\nIf there was nothing there all along.\nMain Riff\nI braved treacherous streets, and kids strung out on homemade speed\nAnd we shared bed in which I could not sleep at all, woo-hoo, woo-hoo\n'Cause at night the sun in retreat made the skyline look like crooked teeth,\n\n[intro]\nYou're so cute when you're slurring your speech,\n(maj7)\n\n[chorus]\n(hold 2) (hold 2)\nI'm war, of head versus heart,\n(hold 2) (hold 2)\nIt's always this way.\n(hold 2) (hold 2)\nMy head is weak, my heart always speaks,\n(hold 2)\n\n[bridge]\nAnd you can't find nothing at all,\nIf there was nothing there all along.\nNo you can't find nothing at all,\nIf there was nothing there all along.\nNo, you can't find nothing at all,\nIf there was nothing there all along.\nThere were churches, theme parks, and malls,\nThere was nothing there all along.",
